{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789408509,"nonce":"FqPGe/Pn7pWHEmXPZn0eebueLd4=","message":"Stage 1 landed: VM is split into Shared (heap, engine and tier state,\nclasses, modules and their variables, interner, config, loaders,\nreload state) behind an Arc'd cell, and VM as one thread's view\n(fiber, api stack, error state, pending fiber action, sync-entry\nfiber and pools, register pool, scheduler world) that derefs to\nShared. VM::new_thread makes another view. The interner-taking\nengine calls got forwarders on Shared so a call site borrows the\nprogram once. Plugins are unaffected: every shipped dylib uses the\nfunction ABI, none reads VM fields. Verified: lib/e2e/hatch_runner/\nkrio suites, e2e under GC stress, AOT suites, tiered corpus 42/42,\nhatch/site; four clippy configs clean; NUC numbers unchanged (fib\n0.42 s, method_call 0.10, binary_trees 0.56, nbody 1.05, generator\n0.30).\n\nNext, stage 2: the heap. Per-thread allocation into Immix blocks\nfrom a shared pool, a stop-the-world that parks every thread view at\na safepoint with its sp published, roots gathered from every view,\nand the epoch-word poll at compiled loop headers so hot code reaches\nthe safepoint.","files":null}]}